            <h3>
              Which of the following is known as the 'Cradle of Indian
              Civilization'?
            </h3>
            <ul class="options">
              <li data-correct="false">Indus Valley</li>
              <li data-correct="true">Harrapan Civilization</li>
              <li data-correct="false">Vedic Period</li>
              <li data-correct="false">Mauryan Empire</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="explanation">
              The Harrapan Civilization is often referred to as the 'Cradle of
              Indian Civilization' due to its early development in the Indus
              Valley.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="questions">
            <h3>Who was the founder of the Maurya Empire?</h3>
            <ul class="options">
              <li data-correct="true">Chandragupta Maurya</li>
              <li data-correct="false">Ashoka</li>
              <li data-correct="false">Bindusara</li>
              <li data-correct="false">Samudragupta</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="explanation">
              Chandragupta Maurya founded the Maurya Empire in ancient India
              around 321 BCE.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="questions">
            <h3>
              Which empire is known for its extensive trade networks and
              cultural exchange?
            </h3>
            <ul class="options">
              <li data-correct="false">Gupta Empire</li>
              <li data-correct="false">Mughal Empire</li>
              <li data-correct="true">Maurya Empire</li>
              <li data-correct="false">Chola Dynasty</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="explanation">
              The Maurya Empire is known for its extensive trade networks and
              cultural exchange with other regions.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="questions">
            <h3>
              Which ancient Indian text is considered the first comprehensive
              grammar?
            </h3>
            <ul class="options">
              <li data-correct="false">Vedas</li>
              <li data-correct="true">Ashtadhyayi</li>
